test.yaml:1:1: workflow has no "concurrency:", so a run that a schedule or a person starts executes at the same time as a run that is still going. add a top-level "concurrency:" with a "group:" such as "${{ github.workflow }}", so that a new run waits for the running one. do not add "cancel-in-progress: true" unless a run can be thrown away without losing work: nothing supersedes such a run, so a cancelled one is not started again. only one run can wait, and a newer run that is waiting replaces the older one that is waiting, so an occurrence can be skipped: add "queue: max" (up to 100 runs wait) when every occurrence must run. for a manual run that takes inputs add them to the group, so that runs with other inputs do not replace each other [concurrency-limits]
